cratic lean, her incumbency, and her cash advantage all point the same direction. Rating outlets and prediction markets uniformly treat the race as out of reach, and the lone single-digit October survey is an outlier against a consistent double-digit pattern.", "watch": "Whether the tight mid-October Pollfinity result signals genuine post-debate tightening rather than pollster noise.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Kathy Hochul (D) is running."]}, "overview": "New York's governor's race pits incumbent Democrat Kathy Hochul against Nassau County Executive Bruce Blakeman. Polling since mid-September has consistently shown Hochul ahead, with most surveys in the 9-to-19-point range and an average near 12 points. The state's Democratic lean, Hochul's incumbency, and her fundraising edge all point the same direction, and rating outlets uniformly place the race in the safest Democratic categories.\n\nBlakeman has kept pace financially, and one late-October poll showed a single-digit race, with the campaign centered on Trump, crime, and bail reform. Even so, no independent evidence suggests the contest is genuinely competitive; prediction markets put Democratic odds above 90 percent. Hochul remains a strong favorite to win a second full term.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 12.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9776, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9779, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9761, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9756, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9778, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9796, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9804, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9807, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.